---Helper type containing information used to filter what ops should be available on a component.
---@class ui.OpNameFilter
---@field filterString string Filtering string to compare against op names.
---@field exactMatch boolean Whether the filter string must be an exact match to the op name, otherwise the filter string is a substring.
---@field invertFilter boolean Inverts the filter results, ie. op names that don't match the filter string return true.
ui.OpNameFilter = {}

---Creates a new op name filter object.
---@return ui.OpNameFilter # The newly created filter, default initialized, or setup with the provided filter string and options.
---@overload fun(filterString: string, exactMatch: boolean, invertFilter: boolean): ui.OpNameFilter
function ui.OpNameFilter.new() end

---Checks if the provided string passes this filter.
---@param testString string String to test this filter against.
---@return boolean # True if the provided string would pass this filter, false otherwise.
function ui.OpNameFilter:Test(testString) end

---Config type containing the ingame actions available for the player to perform when interacting with this config's UI
---component.
---
---Supports filtering ops based on their ID and/or name, as well as marking visible ops as high priority based on their
---ID and/or name.
---@class ui.ComponentOpConfig
---@field pauseText string Text to display for this component when an interface pause is triggered by the server. Only affects text and button components.
---@field opWikiText string Text to display for this component's Wiki op entry in the right-click menu.
---@field numOpNames integer (Read-only) Number of ops defined for this component.
---@field numOpCursors integer (Read-only) Number of cursors defined for this component's ops.
---@field opNames string[] (Read-only) Names for the ops available for this component.
---@field opBaseName string (Read-only) Suffix used for ops for this component. Commonly used to identify the target of an op.
---@field opCursors integer[] (Read-only) IDs for the cursors available for this component's ops.
---@field targetOpVerb string (Read-only) Prefix used for ops for this component when in target mode. Commonly used to identify the action to perform with something.
---@field targetOpCursor integer ID for the cursor to use when in target mode for this component.
local ComponentOpConfig = {}

---Retrieves the name of the op at the specified index.
---@param opIndex integer Index of the op that will be accessed.
---@return string # The name of the specified op, or an empty string if missing.
function ComponentOpConfig:GetOpName(opIndex) end

---Resets the names of all previously defined ops.
---
---Warning: This doesn't affect cursors for the ops, those must be cleared using ClearOpCursors.
function ComponentOpConfig:ClearOpNames() end

---Retrieves the cursor ID of the op at the specified index.
---@param opIndex integer Index of the op that will be accessed.
---@return integer # The cursor ID of the specified op, or `-1` if missing.
function ComponentOpConfig:GetOpCursor(opIndex) end

---Sets the cursor ID of the op at the specified index.
---@param opIndex integer Index of the op that will be accessed.
---@param cursorID integer ID of the cursor to use for this op.
function ComponentOpConfig:SetOpCursor(opIndex, cursorID) end

---Resets the cursors of all previously defined ops.
---
---Warning: This doesn't affect names for the ops, those must be cleared using ClearOpNames.
function ComponentOpConfig:ClearOpCursors() end

---Checks whether or not SetOpIDHidden or SetOpNameHidden have been called previously, resulting in active filters for
---visible ops.
---@return boolean # True if there are any active visible op filters, false otherwise.
function ComponentOpConfig:HasHiddenTests() end

---Tests whether the op at the specified index is hidden or not.
---@param opIndex integer Index of the op that will be accessed.
---@return boolean # True if this op exists and is hidden, false otherwise.
function ComponentOpConfig:TestOpIsHidden(opIndex) end

---Resets both the op name hidden filters and op ID hidden by default settings.
function ComponentOpConfig:ClearHiddenOps() end

---Controls whether the op at the specified index is hidden or not by default.
---@param opIndex integer Index of the op that will be accessed.
---@param hidden boolean Whether this op should be hidden by default or not.
function ComponentOpConfig:SetOpIDHidden(opIndex, hidden) end

---Retrieves whether the op at the specified index is hidden or not by default.
---@param opIndex integer Index of the op that will be accessed.
---@return boolean # True if this op exists and is hidden by default, false otherwise.
function ComponentOpConfig:GetOpIDHidden(opIndex) end

---Sets the filter used to determine if an op is hidden or not based on its name.
---@param filter ui.OpNameFilter Filter used to determine whether an op should be hidden or not based on its name.
function ComponentOpConfig:SetOpNameHidden(filter) end

---Gets the filter used to determine if an op is hidden or not based on its name.
---@return ui.OpNameFilter # Currently active filter used to determine whether an op should be hidden or not based on its name. If not set previously, this will represent an always-pass filter.
function ComponentOpConfig:GetOpNameHidden() end

---Checks whether or not SetOpIDHighPriority or SetOpNameHighPriority have been called previously, resulting in active
---filters for high priority ops.
---@return boolean # True if there are any active high priority op filters, false otherwise.
function ComponentOpConfig:HasHighPriorityTests() end

---Tests whether the op at the specified index is shown higher on the op list or not.
---@param opIndex integer Index of the op that will be accessed.
---@return boolean # True if this op exists and is shown higher on the op list, false otherwise.
function ComponentOpConfig:TestOpIsHighPriority(opIndex) end

---Resets both the op name high priority filters and op ID high priority by default settings.
function ComponentOpConfig:ClearHighPriorityOps() end

---Controls whether the op at the specified index is shown higher on the op list or not by default.
---@param opIndex integer Index of the op that will be accessed.
---@param highPriority boolean Whether this op should be shown higher on the op list by default or not.
function ComponentOpConfig:SetOpIDHighPriority(opIndex, highPriority) end

---Retrieves whether the op at the specified index is shown higher on the op list or not by default.
---@param opIndex integer Index of the op that will be accessed.
---@return boolean # True if this op exists and is shown higher on the op list by default, false otherwise.
function ComponentOpConfig:GetOpIDHighPriority(opIndex) end

---Sets the filter used to determine if an op should be shown higher on the op list or not based on its name.
---@param filter ui.OpNameFilter Filter used to determine whether an op should be shown higher on the op list or not based on its name.
function ComponentOpConfig:SetOpNameHighPriority(filter) end

---Gets the filter used to determine if an op should be shown higher on the op list or not based on its name.
---@return ui.OpNameFilter # Currently active filter used to determine whether an op should be shown higher on the op list or not based on its name. If not set previously, this will represent an always-fail filter.
function ComponentOpConfig:GetOpNameHighPriority() end

---Configuration paremeters used for swipe gesture handling on components.
---@class ui.ComponentSwipeConfig
---@field directionMask integer Combination of ui.SwipeDirectionBit, determines the direction used to detect swipe gestures.
---@field deadZoneHorizontal integer Minimum horizontal travel distance before an input is treated as a swipe gesture.
---@field deadZoneVertical integer Minimum vertical travel distance before an input is treated as a swipe gesture.
---@field deceleration integer Determines how far a swipe gesture drifts based on previous motion. Ranges from `1` to `100`, representing `1%`-`100%` deceleration. A value of `100` results in no swipe drift being applied.
---@field stopExponent integer Exponent applied to the threshold value at which we stop drifting. A value of `1` indicates drifting stops at drift speeds below `0.1`, while `2` results in stopping below `0.01`. Should generally be left at the default value of `8` for consistency.
local ComponentSwipeConfig = {}

---Sets the minimum travel distance for horizontal and vertical inputs before being treated as a swipe gesture.
---@param horizontal integer
---@param vertical integer
function ComponentSwipeConfig:SetDeadZone(horizontal, vertical) end

---Configuration parameters used for drag gestures handling on components.
---@class ui.ComponentDragConfig
---@field draggedComponent ui.Component? The component that's being actively dragged.
---@field renderBehaviour ui.DragRenderBehaviour Indicates how the component should be rendered while it's being dragged.
---@field dragDelayTicks integer How long the user must be attempting a drag action for on a component in logic ticks, before the action actually starts.
---@field deadZone integer Minimum distance in interface units before a drag gesture is triggered, assuming `dragDelayTicks` has been exceeded.

---Configuration parameters used for pinch gestures handling on components.
---@class ui.ComponentPinchConfig
---@field directionMask integer Combination of ui.SwipeDirectionBit, determines the direction used to detect pinch gestures.
---@field threshold integer Minimum distance in interface units before a pinch gesture is triggered.

